{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.CyclotomicDilogCollapse"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDilog_periodic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDilog_periodic","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicQuantumDilog.lean#L148-L159","doc":"Full periodicity under scaling by any power `ζ^j`: `Φ(ζ^j·x) = Φ(x)`. This\nis the \"closes as a finite N-step recursion\" statement — iterating the single\n`ζ`-shift `cyclicDilog_shift` `j` times leaves `Φ` unchanged, so the shift\nrecursion is `N`-periodic (indeed period `1` in the `ζ`-scaling). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDilog_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDilog_shift","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicQuantumDilog.lean#L139-L146","doc":"**Shift invariance of the finite cyclic quantum dilog** `Φ(ζ·x) = Φ(x)` at\nthe root of unity — the finite mirror of the Faddeev shift, with the `(1 + qx)`\nmultiplier absorbed by the cyclic wrap-around. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDenom_prod_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDenom_prod_shift","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicQuantumDilog.lean#L126-L137","doc":"The N-periodicity as an explicit `Finset.prod` reindex statement:\n`∏_{k<N}(1 - x·ζ^{k+1}) = ∏_{k<N}(1 - x·ζ^k)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDenom_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDenom_shift","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicQuantumDilog.lean#L112-L124","doc":"**Exact N-periodicity of the denominator** at the root of unity: scaling the\nargument by `ζ` (a full rotation of the cyclic factor family) leaves the finite\ndenominator invariant. Equivalently, the reindex\n\n    ∏_{k<N}(1 - x·ζ^{k+1}) = ∏_{k<N}(1 - x·ζ^k)\n\nholds because `ζ^N = 1`. Proved via the collapse `cyclicDenom = 1 - x^N`:\n`(ζ·x)^N = ζ^N·x^N = x^N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDenom_shift_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDenom_shift_factor","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicQuantumDilog.lean#L78-L110","doc":"**Finite shift factor law** (the honest finite analog of the Faddeev shift\n`Φ(q²x) = (1 + qx)Φ(x)`). For *every* truncation length `m` — no root-of-unity\nhypothesis — scaling the argument by `ζ` trades the bottom boundary factor\n`(1 - x)` for the top boundary factor `(1 - x·ζ^m)`:\n\n    (1 - x) · cyclicDenom ζ (ζ·x) m  =  (1 - x·ζ^m) · cyclicDenom ζ x m .\n\nBoth sides equal the length-`(m+1)` product `∏_{k=0}^{m}(1 - x·ζ^k)`: the left\nside reconstructs it by prepending the `k = 0` factor to the shifted family, the\nright side by appending the `k = m` factor to the unshifted family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDenom_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDenom_eq","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicQuantumDilog.lean#L70-L76","doc":"**Cyclotomic collapse of the denominator** (corollary of L1\n`cyclotomic_collapse`): at a primitive `N`-th root of unity `ζ` with `N > 0`,\nthe finite q-Pochhammer denominator is the polynomial `1 - x^N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDenom_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDenom_succ","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicQuantumDilog.lean#L65-L68","doc":"Peel the top factor: `(x;ζ)_{N+1} = (x;ζ)_N · (1 - x·ζ^N)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDenom_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDenom_zero","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicQuantumDilog.lean#L62-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDilog","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDilog","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicQuantumDilog.lean#L57-L60","doc":"**Finite cyclic quantum dilogarithm** `Φ(x) = (x;ζ)_N⁻¹`, the reciprocal of\nthe finite q-Pochhammer denominator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDenom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.CyclicQuantumDilog.cyclicDenom","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/CyclicQuantumDilog.lean#L51-L55","doc":"**Finite q-Pochhammer denominator** `(x;ζ)_N = ∏_{k=0}^{N-1}(1 - x·ζ^k)`.\nThis is the finite root-of-unity truncation of the analytic q-Pochhammer\ndenominator; by `cyclicDenom_eq` it collapses to the polynomial `1 - x^N`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}